Subject: Re: New integration — next steps and cutover window

Alex / team — attaching a minimal endpoint migration script and two sample snippets (Node + Python). Key notes included below.

Attachment list: sdk-sample-configs.zip (contains migration-script.sh, node-sample.js, python-sample.py)

Migration pattern (safe, canary-first):
- Step 0: Warm KV cache in staging (run a 10k token workload to populate prefixes).
- Step 1: Deploy SDK config change to point to the /v2/stream endpoint with header X-RW-Variant: stable-canary.
- Step 2: Route 5% traffic for 20 minutes, verify p95 latency and error rates.
- Step 3: Ramp 5 -> 25 -> 60% with 30m observation windows.
- Step 4: Full cutover when signals are green.

Retries/timeouts guidance:
- Client timeout: default 60s for generation calls; reduce to 20s for short prompt flows.
- Retry policy: idempotent-only auto-retries (embeddings, reranks). For non-idempotent generation: use at-most-once by default; retries only on explicit 5xx after a 20s backoff.

Sample Node snippet (from node-sample.js):
const Redwood = require('@redwood-ai/sdk');
const client = new Redwood.Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, baseUrl: 'https://api.redwood.ai/v2' });

async function migrateRequest() {
  try {
    const res = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-lite-7b', input: 'translate: Hello' , timeout: 20000 });
    console.log(res.output[0].content);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === 429) {
      // apply exponential jittered backoff
    } else {
      throw err;
    }
  }
}

Rollback triggers we recommend:
- >2x baseline 5xx rate during canary,
- p95 latency regression > 300ms,
- KV cache miss rate rises > 40%

I'll be available for a short technical dry run on Thursday 2027-04-29 17:00 UTC.

— Vivek
